# Simulation: Mix two solutions 1:1
# After mixing: 25 mmol/kg C and 25 mmol/kg Ca
# But the question asks about moles in the mixture (2 kg water total)
# Let's try with the mixed solution having 50 mmol/kg each (no dilution interpretation)
# i.e., each solution contributes 50 mmol to 1 kg of mixed water

SOLUTION 1
    temp      20
    pH        7.0
    C(4)      50 mmol/kgw
    Ca        50 mmol/kgw
    units     mmol/kgw

EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1
    Calcite   0.0   0.0

REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1
    20.0  38.0  56.0  74.0  92.0  110.0  128.0  146.0  164.0  182.0  200.0

SELECTED_OUTPUT
    -file   mixing_heating4.sel
    -reset  false
    -temperature true
    -equilibrium_phases Calcite

END
